      "claim": "The hierarchy driver's generated CHECK (set -eu; mkdir -p .scratch/bend2; python3 \"$1\") runs the selected test file directly instead of the bend2/scripts/check-unittest.sh adapter. In a fresh fixture tree with bend2/ copied in and .scratch/bend2/baton2 absent, /bin/sh <CHECK> bend2/test/receive.py exited 0 with empty stdout and stderr 'Ran 28 tests in 0.000s / OK (skipped=28)': every Receive test skipped because the coordinator was absent, so no test body executed while the checked-landing gate would record a passing check.",
